 {r}←key AddDependencyTarget(ref target);name;targetKey;msg;folder;oldTarget;tmp
⍝ Adds the target namespace `target` to the "tatin" or "nuget" dependency setting in the namespace `ref`.
⍝ `key` names the setting, e.g. 'dependencies_dev.tatin'; see `ParseDependencySetting` for details.
⍝ `ref` is changed in place, in the form the setting already uses: when there is a "tatinTarget"
⍝ ("nugetTarget") the target goes there; otherwise it is added to "tatin" ("nuget") as '<folder>=<target>'.
⍝ Signals an error when the setting is invalid, defines no folder or has a target namespace already,
⍝ and when `target` is not a valid target namespace. `ref` is not changed then.
⍝ The shy result is always 1.
 r←1
 name←key↓⍨key⍳'.'
 targetKey←name,'Target'
 (msg folder oldTarget)←key ParseDependencySetting ref
 msg Assert 0=≢msg
 ('No folder is defined in "',key,'"; cannot add a target namespace')Assert 0<≢folder
 ('There is already a target namespace defined in "',key,'"; edit the project config file to change that')Assert 0=≢oldTarget
⍝ Compose the new setting in a scratch namespace and check it before `ref` is touched
 tmp←⎕NS''
 :If 0<ref.⎕NC targetKey
     ⍎'tmp.',name,'←folder'
     ⍎'tmp.',targetKey,'←target'
 :Else
     ⍎'tmp.',name,'←ComposeDependencySetting folder target'
 :EndIf
 msg←⊃key ParseDependencySetting tmp
 msg Assert 0=≢msg
 :If 0<ref.⎕NC targetKey
     ⍎'ref.',targetKey,'←target'
 :Else
     ⍎'ref.',name,'←tmp.',name
 :EndIf
⍝Done
